<title>UK: Waddington H1 pretax climbs 35.7 percent.</title>
<headline>Waddington H1 pretax climbs 35.7 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 28</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		 10.54		 vs   7.90</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	   4.4		  vs   4.0</p>
<p> Pretax			15.5		  vs  11.5</p>
<p> Turnover		   155.6		  vs 131.7</p>
<p> Interest		    0.87		  vs   0.34</p>
<p> Tax			   4.51		  vs   3.21</p>
<p> Net taxed		  11.04		  vs   8.25</p>
<p>NOTE - Specialist manufacturer and packaging group Waddington Plc, formerly known as John Waddington Plc, said strong demand was behind the increase in turnover, and profit growth was helped by recent restructuring. It said it was confident of continued growth in the year to March 1997.</p>
<p>The company did not announce the payment and registration dates in regard to dividend payout.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44-171-542 7717</p>
</text>
